	<p align="justify">The speaker selection is the heart of any sound system design, be it a concert hall, a church, or a classroom. Soundbars can be a wonderful solution to installation and space issues, but that typical soundbar from your local audio or discount store was designed for a living room or residential entertainment system. With maybe 6 kids on a busy Saturday, youâ€™re probably OK with that in your 200 sq. ft. home TV room, but a US classroom is typically 5 times larger than the average residential living room.</p>
